{"status":"ready","content":"We are given the sample: \\(\\{1, -21, -21, -18, 8\\}\\).\n\nLet's compute the **sample standard deviation** step by step.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Compute the Sample Mean\n\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{1 + (-21) + (-21) + (-18) + 8}{5} = \\frac{1 - 21 - 21 - 18 + 8}{5} = \\frac{-51}{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 2. Compute Each Squared Deviation\n\nCalculate each \\((x_i - \\bar{x})^2\\):\n\n#### For \\(x_1 = 1\\):\n\n\\[\nx_1 - \\bar{x} = 1 - \\left(-\\frac{51}{5}\\right) = 1 + \\frac{51}{5} = \\frac{56}{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_1 - \\bar{x})^2 = \\left(\\frac{56}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{3136}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### For \\(x_2 = -21\\):\n\n\\[\nx_2 - \\bar{x} = -21 - \\left(-\\frac{51}{5}\\right) = -21 + \\frac{51}{5} = \\frac{-105 + 51}{5} = \\frac{-54}{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_2 - \\bar{x})^2 = \\left(\\frac{-54}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{2916}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### For \\(x_3 = -21\\) (same as above):\n\n\\[\n(x_3 - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{2916}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### For \\(x_4 = -18\\):\n\n\\[\nx_4 - \\bar{x} = -18 - \\left(-\\frac{51}{5}\\right) = -18 + \\frac{51}{5} = \\frac{-90 + 51}{5} = \\frac{-39}{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_4 - \\bar{x})^2 = \\left(\\frac{-39}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1521}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### For \\(x_5 = 8\\):\n\n\\[\nx_5 - \\bar{x} = 8 - \\left(-\\frac{51}{5}\\right) = 8 + \\frac{51}{5} = \\frac{40 + 51}{5} = \\frac{91}{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_5 - \\bar{x})^2 = \\left(\\frac{91}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{8281}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 3. Sum the Squared Deviations\n\nAdd all these up:\n\n\\[\n\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{3136}{25} + \\frac{2916}{25} + \\frac{2916}{25} + \\frac{1521}{25} + \\frac{8281}{25}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{3136 + 2916 + 2916 + 1521 + 8281}{25}\n\\]\n\nFirst sum the numerators:\n\\[\n3136 + 2916 = 6052 \n\\]\n\\[\n6052 + 2916 = 8968\n\\]\n\\[\n8968 + 1521 = 10489\n\\]\n\\[\n10489 + 8281 = 18770\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\\[\n\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{18770}{25}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 4. Divide by \\(n-1 = 5-1 = 4\\):\n\n\\[\ns^2 = \\frac{1}{n-1} \\sum 